        "panel": {
          "introduction": "Apophis is a near-Earth asteroid with a preliminary radar reconstruction. This view uses the published Model B at its original scale. Explore its original shape and radial heights. The grid marks unavailable surface imagery. The weak 2012–2013 radar data admit multiple shapes; the 2026 PDS release preserves the 2018 Model B rather than a new reconstruction. Apophis tumbles: the archived precession and rotation periods are 27.45 and 265.7 hours. This view uses a fixed illustrative frame, without propagating its tumbling attitude. No optical surface map is supplied.",
